{
  "_comment": [
    "Pinned sidecar downloads for scripts/fetch-binaries.ps1 and scripts/fetch-binaries.sh.",
    "Each sidecar is saved as src-tauri/binaries/<name>-<target-triple>[.exe], matching externalBin in src-tauri/tauri.conf.json.",
    "'triples' maps a Rust target triple to a platform key under each sidecar.",
    "sha256 is the hash of the downloaded file. Every download is verified: a mismatch, or a pinned entry with an empty sha256, fails the script.",
    "'pinned': false is only allowed as a temporary state; the scripts then print a loud warning with the computed hash.",
    "yt-dlp hashes come from the release's SHA2-256SUMS file. ffmpeg hashes come from the release's SHA256SUMS.txt.",
    "QuickJS-NG v0.18.0 publishes no SHA256SUMS file; its hashes are the sha256 digests GitHub lists for each release asset."
